# 15 Pattern conversion: pcre2_pattern_convert()
# https://www.pcre.org/current/doc/html/pcre2convert.html
#
# Not exposed by PHP.
#
# What it is: a converter that turns foreign pattern dialects into
# equivalent PCRE2 patterns. It understands shell globs and both POSIX
# regex flavors. The #pattern convert=glob command below makes pcre2test
# convert every following pattern and print the translation right after
# compiling it.
#
# What it enables: accepting glob or POSIX syntax at an API boundary
# (file filters, legacy configs) while matching with one engine. The
# hand-written glob-to-regex translator in userland goes away.

#pattern convert=glob

# Expect: (?s)\Aa(*COMMIT)[^/]*?c\.txt\z
#         then 0: abc.txt
# The glob a*c.txt is converted (pcre2test prints the translation) and
# compiled. * does not cross '/' and the dot is literal and the whole
# thing is anchored. Glob semantics with no userland translation code.
/a*c.txt/
    abc.txt

# Expect: (?s)\Aa(*COMMIT)[^/]*?c\.txt\z
#         then No match
# The '/' in "ab/c.txt" is exactly what * must not cross, so the glob
# does not match. The translation prints again because this block
# compiles the glob afresh.
/a*c.txt/
    ab/c.txt
